+# Deploying the Static IPFS Build
+
+This repo is configured for a static Next.js export when `NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true`. Do not upload from automation unless you intend to publish; the commands below are the exact manual workflow.
+
+## 1. Deploy the Contract on Base
+
+Set a real recipient before deploying to Base. This costs real gas.
+
+```bash
+export BASE_RPC_URL="https://base-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/YOUR_KEY"
+export TIP_JAR_RECIPIENT="0xYourRecipientAddress"
+
+TIP_JAR_RECIPIENT="$TIP_JAR_RECIPIENT" yarn deploy --network base
+```
+
+Confirm that `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts` now includes chain id `8453` and `BaseUsdcTipJar`.
+
+## 2. Clean Static Build
+
+Replace the production URL with the gateway or ENS URL users will share.
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+rm -rf .next out
+
+NEXT_PUBLIC_TARGET_NETWORK=base \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL="$BASE_RPC_URL" \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL="https://yourapp.yourname.eth.link" \
+NODE_OPTIONS="--require ./polyfill-localstorage.cjs" \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_IGNORE_BUILD_ERROR=true \
+yarn build
+```
+
+Pre-upload checks:
+
+```bash
+ls out/*/index.html
+grep 'og:image' out/index.html
+grep -R "Base USDC Tip Jar" out/index.html out/_next/static/chunks
+stat -f '%Sm' app/page.tsx
+stat -f '%Sm' out
+```
+
+## 3. Upload to IPFS
+
+Run this only when you are ready to publish the exact contents of `packages/nextjs/out`.
+
+```bash
+yarn bgipfs upload config init -u https://upload.bgipfs.com
+CID=$(yarn bgipfs upload out | tee /tmp/base-usdc-tipjar-ipfs.log | sed -n 's/.*CID: //p' | head -n 1)
+echo "$CID"
+```
+
+## 4. Verify the Gateway
+
+```bash
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "https://community.bgipfs.com/ipfs/$CID/"
+curl -s -L "https://community.bgipfs.com/ipfs/$CID/" | grep 'og:image'
+curl -s -L "https://community.bgipfs.com/ipfs/$CID/" | grep "Base USDC Tip Jar"
+```
+
+Each command should return a healthy result: HTTP `200`, an absolute `og:image`, and the app title in the HTML or static chunks.
+
+## 5. Optional ENS Contenthash
+
+After reviewing the gateway URL, set the ENS content hash to:
+
+```text
+ipfs://$CID
+```
+
+Then verify onchain:
+
+```bash
+export ENS_NAME="yourapp.yourname.eth"
+export RESOLVER=$(cast call 0x00000000000C2e074eC69A0dFb2997BA6C7d2e1e \
+  "resolver(bytes32)(address)" "$(cast namehash "$ENS_NAME")" \
+  --rpc-url https://eth.llamarpc.com)
+
+cast call "$RESOLVER" "contenthash(bytes32)(bytes)" \
+  "$(cast namehash "$ENS_NAME")" --rpc-url https://eth.llamarpc.com
+
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "https://$ENS_NAME.link"
+```
